        <body>
            <div xml:id="d626">

                <pb facs="1089" n="989" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg989"/>

                <head>No. 626.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Heap.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-09-22"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 22,
                        1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 273.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your cipher telegram, dated at
                    Constantinople the 17thinstant, has been received. It reads as follows, viz:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Legal counsel necessary prosecution of murderers. Do you authorize
                            it?</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Upon the 20th instant the Department replied thereto as follows, viz: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>You are authorized to employ counsel.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>These telegrams are understood to relate to the case of Dr. Parsons and servant
                    recently murdered near Ismid, in Turkey.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
